            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for prayer, then the Arabic for a relationship."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: معا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "معا — maʿan — \"together\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "معا (maʿan) is maʿa, \"with\", with the adverb ending -an: \"together\". Lane lists maʿa as an old particle; Hebrew ʿim, \"with\", is usually compared."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
